<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:36:05 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Lebanon: UNIFIL withdrawal at the heart of Paris talks</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-unifil-withdrawal-at-the-heart-of-paris-talks</link><description>
Emmanuel Macron welcomes Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II to Paris today for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as France pushes to prevent a security vacuum ahead of UNIFIL's planned withdrawal at the end of 2026, with Israeli strikes continuing in southern Lebanon and concerns growing over who will secure the border. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d493f712-b297-11f1-8ba9-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-130744-131215-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d493f712-b297-11f1-8ba9-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-130744-131215-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9f5b718-b297-11f1-92f4-d3e82812b02d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:23:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Syrian court issues first sentences over 2025 massacres of Alawites</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-syrian-court-issues-first-sentences-over-2025-massacres-of-alawites</link><description>
Syria's judiciary on Thursday issued its first verdicts over the massacres of Alawites on the Syrian coast last year, sentencing a former member of government forces to 20 years in prison. A supporter of deposed president Bashar al-Assad received a death sentence and another was sentenced to life in jail. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fe5ee0-414b-11f0-b396-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36ZR2LG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fe5ee0-414b-11f0-b396-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36ZR2LG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48306f1c-b274-11f1-b38e-275430d05d0c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:13:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fe5ee0-414b-11f0-b396-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36ZR2LG.jpg">© Delil Souleiman, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon: Emmanuel Macron welcomes Joseph Aoun to Paris for Middle East talks</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-emmanuel-macron-welcomes-joseph-aoun-to-paris-for-middle-east-talks</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun in Paris for talks focused on Lebanon's security and wider Middle East tensions, with Jordan's King Abdullah II also taking part in the meeting. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago and Kethevane Gorjestani have the analysis from Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c694a296-b270-11f1-b93b-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-100132-101156-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c694a296-b270-11f1-b93b-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-100132-101156-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb7932a4-b270-11f1-b8db-a5077b1dbff6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:48:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon: Macron, Aoun and King Abdullah II hold security talks in Paris</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-macron-aoun-and-king-abdullah-ii-hold-security-talks-in-paris</link><description>
Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II in Paris for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as concerns grow over Israel's continued strikes in southern Lebanon and the possible end of the UNIFIL peacekeeping mission, with France seeking a "clear, credible and realistic" plan to back Lebanon through funding, equipment and military training.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/422cc902-b26b-11f1-83de-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090233-090415-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/422cc902-b26b-11f1-83de-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090233-090415-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ad76774-b26b-11f1-89f3-e9e6715e3397</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:59:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East : Trump plans $2.8bn arms package for Israel amid Gaza war</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-trump-plans-2-8bn-arms-package-for-israel-amid-gaza-war</link><description>
The Trump administration is reportedly preparing a $2.8 billion arms package for Israel, including 40,000 bombs, as Israel continues strikes in Gaza despite last October's ceasefire. The proposed deal would further strengthen Israel's military capabilities and revive deliveries of 2,000-pound bombs that had previously been paused over concerns about civilian casualties.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/634b4612-b26c-11f1-b404-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090447-090628-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/634b4612-b26c-11f1-b404-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-090447-090628-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68e45492-b26c-11f1-b49c-391e5dc51093</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:55:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Paris talks aim to bolster Lebanese army as end of UN mission looms</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-middle-east-live-paris-talks-lebanese-army-unifil-israel-iran-yemen</link><description>
European and Arab military chiefs meet in Paris on Thursday to discuss steps to bolster Lebanon's struggling armed forces as the mandate of a United Nations peacekeeping mission expires at the end of the year, amid fears of a renewed Israeli military campaign in southern Lebanon. Follow our live coverage for updates from the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6d6a6e6-b264-11f1-b43e-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T064902Z-1226377853-RC2UKNA3EWKJ-RTRMADP-3-LEBANON-CRISIS-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6d6a6e6-b264-11f1-b43e-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T064902Z-1226377853-RC2UKNA3EWKJ-RTRMADP-3-LEBANON-CRISIS-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3972b62c-b25d-11f1-ba05-4ffa55b88d33</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:14:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6d6a6e6-b264-11f1-b43e-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T064902Z-1226377853-RC2UKNA3EWKJ-RTRMADP-3-LEBANON-CRISIS-FRANCE.jpg">© Abdul Saboor, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel and Morocco agree to open embassies after New York talks</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-israel-morocco-embassies-new-york</link><description>
Israel and Morocco agreed on Wednesday to open embassies in each other’s countries following talks between their foreign ministers and the US ambassador to the United Nations in New York. The two countries established diplomatic ties in 2020 under the US-brokered Abraham Accords, which normalised Israel’s relations with several Arab states.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89d8337a-b209-11f1-9497-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23249705702543-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89d8337a-b209-11f1-9497-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23249705702543-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e101552-b221-11f1-b75a-3be68007f0a3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:07:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89d8337a-b209-11f1-9497-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23249705702543-1.jpg">© Mosa'ab Elshamy, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Ed Sheeran's tour in trouble after opening acts drop out in solidarity with rapper Macklemore</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-opening-acts-drop-out-in-solidarity-with-rapper-macklemore</link><description>
Ed Sheeran's tour of North and South America has been roiled by the decision this week to drop Macklemore as an opener because of the rapper's onstage pro-Palestinian comments. Since then, all of Sheeran's other supporting acts have dropped out, including a group that backs Sheeran up during part of the show. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with David Jackson, Professor of Political Science at Bowling Green State University about the issue.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289eec80-b212-11f1-9582-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-223104-224345-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289eec80-b212-11f1-9582-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-223104-224345-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">486cdd02-b216-11f1-ac7e-e74f65dccbc1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:33:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ed Sheeran's tour in trouble after opening acts drop out in solidarity with rapper Macklemore</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-opening-acts-drop-out-in-solidarity-with-rapper-macklemore</link><description>
Ed Sheeran's tour of North and South America has been roiled by the decision this week to drop Macklemore as an opener because of the rapper's onstage pro-Palestinian comments. Since then, all of Sheeran's other supporting acts have dropped out, including a group that backs Sheeran up during part of the show. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with David Jackson, Professor of Political Science at Bowling Green State University about the issue.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289eec80-b212-11f1-9582-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-223104-224345-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/289eec80-b212-11f1-9582-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-223104-224345-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e4064b6-b212-11f1-a6ef-b54447e21b73</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:31:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Amnesty says Iran committed 'crimes against humanity' in protests crackdown</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/amnesty-says-iran-committed-crimes-against-humanity-in-protests-crackdown</link><description>
Iranian authorities committed crimes against humanity in the crackdown on 2022 protests that left hundreds dead, Amnesty International said Wednesday, adding Tehran's suppression of new demonstrations this year bore the "same hallmarks" but on an even wider scale. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Amnesty International Iran Researcher Raha Bahreini. She calls for the establishment of an international criminal justice mechanism to prosecute those responsible for the crimes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0fc1bd2-b208-11f1-b188-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-213118-213957-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0fc1bd2-b208-11f1-b188-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-213118-213957-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6ac8bde-b208-11f1-a8b6-b590cfce5101</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:09:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia accuses Houthis of targeting Mecca, calls it a 'red line'</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-saudi-arabia-accuses-houthis-of-targeting-mecca-calling-it-a-red-line</link><description>
Saudi Arabia accused Yemen’s Houthis on Wednesday of launching an attack on the holy city of Mecca, which the Iran-backed rebels denied. Saudi Arabia, a US ally which has been the target of large-scale Houthi strikes since early September, declared Mecca a “red line” as it slid deeper into the new front of the Iran war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/824ac65c-b206-11f1-83d2-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8H2794.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/824ac65c-b206-11f1-83d2-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8H2794.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2d6ae492-b200-11f1-a3a7-0f4fc758a6c4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:08:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/824ac65c-b206-11f1-83d2-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8H2794.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia accuses Houthis of targeting Mecca, warns of 'red line'</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-accuses-houthis-of-targeting-mecca-warns-of-red-line</link><description>
Saudi Arabia accused Yemen's Houthis on Wednesday of launching a "cowardly" attack targeting Islam's holy city of Mecca, sparking outrage across the Muslim world. The Houthis swiftly rejected as a "lie" Riyadh's statement that it had shot down a drone heading towards Mecca, which attracts millions of pilgrims each year. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b49831a-5730-11f1-b727-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26142709290637.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b49831a-5730-11f1-b727-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26142709290637.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0572697c-b202-11f1-8718-db5ba3fdb880</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:13:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Washington set to approve $2.8 bn arms package for Israel</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/washington-set-to-approve-2-8-bn-arms-package-for-israel</link><description>
The US federal government is on track to approve a $2.8 billion arms package for Israel, US media reported Tuesday, with the sale of 40,000 one-ton bombs among the largest munitions packages sold in recent years. The Washington Post said the package -- funded with US taxpayer dollars -- featured some of the most destructive munitions in Western arsenals, including 20,000 MK-84s, 20,000 BLU-117s, and 20,000 I-2000 Penetrator warheads. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/942153e2-b1fb-11f1-bd55-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17306261656aaade6612d4f8-79538850.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/942153e2-b1fb-11f1-bd55-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17306261656aaade6612d4f8-79538850.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e26b3bc-b1fa-11f1-bd40-b312af735817</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:24:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Emergency doctor on the challenges of caring for civilians in conflict zones</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260916-emergency-doctor-on-the-challenges-of-caring-for-civilians-in-conflict-zones</link><description>
For humanitarian doctors and healthcare workers operating in active conflict zones, the challenges are seemingly endless: from so-called "double tap" strikes that put emergency workers at risk, to roadblocks, evacuation orders and even the positioning of humanitarian organisations in the political debate. Pierre Catoire, emergency doctor and vice-president of Mehad – A French NGO dedicated to healthcare in conflict zones – speaks to FRANCE 24 about how medical professionals go about their work in such conditions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c3a232e-b1bd-11f1-9872-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260916-1015-Live-CS1015.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c3a232e-b1bd-11f1-9872-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260916-1015-Live-CS1015.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f89b6cc4-b1bd-11f1-a31e-11ba3a3e976d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:55:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Carys GARLAND</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Amnesty says Iran committed 'crimes against humanity' in 2022 protests crackdown</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-amnesty-international-says-iran-committed-crimes-against-humanity-in-2022-protests-crackdown</link><description>
In a report released Wednesday, Amnesty International said Iranian authorities committed “crimes against humanity” during the violent crackdown on the 2022 protests known as the movement “Woman, Life, Freedom” that was sparked by the death of Mahsa Amini.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa676064-b1b1-11f1-9e38-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32M77DV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa676064-b1b1-11f1-9e38-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32M77DV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34c09a24-b1b1-11f1-84e5-cd7763d25794</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:30:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa676064-b1b1-11f1-9e38-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/000-32M77DV.jpg">© AFP, X</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis report Saudi strikes as Riyadh accuses them of targeting Mecca</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-middle-east-live-saudi-arabia-accuses-houthi-rebels-of-launching-a-drone-strike-on-mecca</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis reported fresh Saudi airstrikes on Wednesday, as Riyadh accused the group of launching a "cowardly" attack targeting Islam's holy city of Mecca. The Houthis swiftly rejected as a "lie" Riyadh's early morning statement that it had shot down a drone heading towards Mecca, but the accusation prompted a chorus of outrage from around the Muslim world. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e76953e8-b218-11f1-8a7d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T134945Z-1339566980-RC2DKNANTNM5-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e76953e8-b218-11f1-8a7d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T134945Z-1339566980-RC2DKNANTNM5-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">589f5008-b174-11f1-bf7c-cffccd86975a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:14:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e76953e8-b218-11f1-8a7d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T134945Z-1339566980-RC2DKNANTNM5-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Houthi Military Media, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi crown prince seeks neighbours' backing as Houthi attacks rattle Red Sea oil routes</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/saudi-crown-prince-seeks-neighbours-backing-as-houthi-attacks-rattle-red-sea-oil-routes</link><description>
Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman and Egyptian President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi called for free and secure navigation in the Red Sea during talks in Cairo on Tuesday, as the kingdom vowed to respond "firmly" to attacks by Yemen's Houthis. The two regional powers discussed the threat posed by the Iran-backed group's control over the Bab al-Mandab Strait. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2dc7031c-b133-11f1-85df-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-201351-201546-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2dc7031c-b133-11f1-85df-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-201351-201546-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75f584ec-b133-11f1-a540-072a85fb6bfd</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:37:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>First Hormuz, now the Red Sea? Oil spikes as Saudis sucked into Yemen spiral</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260915-first-hormuz-now-the-red-sea-oil-spikes-as-saudis-sucked-into-yemen-spiral</link><description>
First, there was US President Donald Trump’s surprise decision to strike Iran. Then, came the quagmire of a war without an exit strategy. Now, six months later, with access to the Strait of Hormuz all but shut, global shipping has taken another hit the other end of the Arabian Peninsula. Iran-backed Houthis are threatening access to the Red Sea. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e00a5de-b12f-11f1-ad88-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T133537Z-76574084-RC2PJNARVJ8Y-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-EGYPT-SAUDI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e00a5de-b12f-11f1-ad88-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-15T133537Z-76574084-RC2PJNARVJ8Y-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-EGYPT-SAUDI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b69efdc-b12f-11f1-9d4c-05a0aff03bd7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:32:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia vows to hit back ‘firmly’ after Houthi attacks</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia</link><description>
Saudi Arabia vowed on Tuesday to respond "firmly" to attacks by Yemen's Houthis after the Iran-backed fighters wounded 13 people in the kingdom’s south following a series of drone and missile attacks. Tensions have escalated since the Houthis pushed their offensive in Yemen and began targeting Riyadh’s ships in the Red Sea. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42024f72-b07e-11f1-8db3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84H89F.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42024f72-b07e-11f1-8db3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84H89F.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">81d8b47c-b0b2-11f1-b0b2-c3058f5430ea</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 03:06:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42024f72-b07e-11f1-8db3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84H89F.jpg">© Mohammed Huwais, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Rights group accuses Israel of dismantling 'Palestinian existence' in West Bank</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/rights-group-accuses-israel-of-dismantling-palestinian-existence-in-west-bank</link><description>
Israeli rights group B'Tselem said Monday that Israeli actions in the occupied West Bank form part of a greater project designed to make it impossible for Palestinians to exist together as a people. In a report titled "The Elimination Project", the group alleged five connected Israeli tactics and policies in the West Bank: "violence, ethnic cleansing, movement restrictions, economic strangulation, social and political destruction". FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5d3dc4-b080-11f1-8b78-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-230418-230604-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5d3dc4-b080-11f1-8b78-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-230418-230604-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4964844-b080-11f1-bc80-69c181e861bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:26:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Yemen: Fact-checking videos claiming to show Houthi rebel attacks</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fact-checking-videos-claiming-to-show-houthi-rebel-attacks-1</link><description>
A video claiming to show Houthi rebels ambushing Saudi-backed mercenaries has racked up major views on X. But the FRANCE 24 Observers found it is actually footage of 2024 Houthi military drills. The clip was edited with football commentary and blurred flags, which originally show Israel, the UK and US, not Saudi Arabia. Other viral videos falsely linked to Houthi attacks on a Saudi Aramco refinery were also traced to unrelated fires in Texas and Russia. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/799a26da-b07e-11f1-9b60-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6257860516aa85f0346da31-02858738.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/799a26da-b07e-11f1-9b60-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6257860516aa85f0346da31-02858738.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f9ccada-b07e-11f1-a49c-69c181e861bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:10:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Axis of Iranian centrality' remains "one of more destabilising forces in the region", expert says</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/axis-of-iranian-centrality-remains-one-of-more-destabilising-forces-in-the-region-expert-says</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis launched a fresh barrage of missile and drone attacks on Saudi military targets on Monday, as Iran denied any involvement in the country's revived civil war. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr H. A. Hellyer, Senior Fellow in Geopolitics, International Security, and Middle East Studies at the Royal United Services Institute, says that Iran and its non-state proxies "remain to be one of the more destabilising forces in the region alongside the Israeli project of regional paramountcy".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/001ebad8-b073-11f1-a1cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-210414-211512-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/001ebad8-b073-11f1-a1cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-210414-211512-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0590cab0-b073-11f1-8e4b-f178ef1761fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:46:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis and Saudi Arabia renew fighting, Iran denies any interference</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-houthis-and-saudi-arabia-renew-fighting-iran-denies-any-interference</link><description>
Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes on western Yemen on Monday after Iran-backed Houthi rebels attacked military facilities in the kingdom. The renewed fighting around the Red Sea comes as the wider US-Iran war threatens vital shipping routes across the region.
